From d4fe0e591e855adbc61ba4746b8a3f0d2bbaa82d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 02:09:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Draw the start-sheet map with Google and search it with
 Google Places

The start sheet searched OpenStreetMap (Photon + Nominatim) because the map
under it was Apple's, and the Places terms keep Google Places content off
a non-Google map. The app ships as its own binary now, which can bundle
the Google Maps SDK, so the map becomes Google's and the search, and the
caption under the map, can come from Google too.

- app.config.js injects GOOGLE_MAPS_IOS_KEY / GOOGLE_MAPS_ANDROID_KEY at
  build time; app.json stays static and key-free.
- MiniMap asks for the Google provider and refuses to render where it
  cannot work (Expo Go on iOS, or a build made without the key).
- fetch-place `search` takes an optional point to bias towards and a
  language; a new `reverse` action names a point via the Geocoding API,
  with the parser in a pure module tested from Node.
- findplace/spots now shape Google candidates; find-address and its OSM
  parsers are removed (the deployed function still needs deleting).
- README, tech-eval and store notes updated; the reviewer letter's "No
  Google Maps SDK is bundled" is flagged as out of date for the next
  submission.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
